    assert!(gj6.contains("The pilot question set stands in examples/pilot/questions.json as a list of twelve objects, each holding a question field with a non empty string and an answers field with two to four offered answers. Every question is synthetic and written for this repo, and the subject matter is plain and everyday. Each question is put to five seats per model, the seats labelled jev-1 to jev-5 for the Jev route and openai-1 to openai-5 for the chat route, so the pilot holds sixty responses per model before abstentions and failed calls. Each question with its responses forms one recorded poll, and the twelve polls stand in examples/pilot as poll-01.json to poll-12.json in question order, each one loading clean under GJ-1 as extended by this section. The first poll also stands at examples/pilot_poll.json as the round example poll, with its golden stadium view at examples/pilot-stadium-golden.txt and its golden cost report at examples/pilot-cost-golden.txt, the cost report rendered from the price table at examples/pilot-prices.json.\n\nThe raw envelopes the live run returned stand in examples/pilot/envelopes, one file per returned envelope, named by question and seat in the form q01-jev-1.json and its fellows. A call that returned no envelope leaves no file, and the run record carries the count of such calls. The script examples/make_pilot.py rebuilds the twelve polls, the example poll, and both goldens from the questions file and the recorded envelopes through the seat readers, entirely offline, and running it against the recorded fixtures reproduces the committed files byte for byte.\n\nThe run record stands at examples/pilot/run_record.json and holds the question count, the seats per question per model, and one record per model string. A model record holds its route name, the calls attempted, the calls recorded, the failed calls, the abstained count among its recorded responses, and the input and output token totals summed over every envelope the route returned, envelopes the reader failed included, because those tokens were spent. The chat route record also holds the dollar cost summed the same way from the usage figure each envelope reports, rendered as a decimal string. The Jev route reports no dollar figure, so its record holds no dollar field.\n\nThe price table at examples/pilot-prices.json prices the chat route model at its measured cost per recorded response in the pilot run, the summed dollar cost of its recorded responses divided by their count, rendered as a decimal string at six decimal places with halves rounding up, and a test recomputes that price from the recorded envelopes. The Jev model stands absent from the table, so its responses stand in the cost report as unpriced responses named with their model and count, exactly as GJ-4 provides, because its route reports no dollar figure to price from.\n\nEvery test in this round runs offline against the recorded envelopes and the recorded polls, and no test makes a live call. Test, tests/test_seats.py, tests/test_pilot.py, and tests/test_examples.py."));
