    let gj8 = contract_section(&text, "### GJ-8 full form, the agreement reading");
    assert!(gj8.contains("The agreement reading is computed over a list of valid polls by the agreement_lines function in the grandjury.agreement module. It takes the polls in the order given and returns the reading as lines, and it is a pure function of its inputs. The command line surface gains a fourth command beside the three the Round 1 section names. The agreement command takes one or more poll files, loads each one in the order given under GJ-1 as extended, and prints the reading of the polls in that order. The first file that draws defects prints invalid poll and its defects in the form the other commands use, and the command exits with status one and prints no reading. A clean run exits with status zero.\n\nA jury in a poll is one model string standing in the poll responses, and the juries of a poll stand in the order their model strings first appear in the responses. The reading holds one section per poll in the order the polls stand, and a closing line after the last section.\n\nA section opens with the question line in the form the tally uses, the word question, a comma, and the question itself. One block then stands per jury. The jury line names the word jury, the model string, and then four counts, each as its word and then its figure, in the order recorded, valid, abstained, and spoiled, in the comma spaced style of the tally lines. Recorded counts every response the jury holds in the poll, valid counts those that are neither abstained nor spoiled, abstained counts the jury responses carrying the abstained field, and spoiled counts those that are not abstained and name an answer that was not offered.\n\nUnder the jury line one line stands per offered answer in offered order, indented by two spaces. The line names the answer, its count among the jury valid responses, its share, and its percentage, in that order. The share is the exact fraction of the jury valid responses that chose the answer, held as an exact fraction and never as a rounded float, and rendered in lowest terms as the numerator, a slash, and the denominator, with a denominator of one rendering as the numerator alone. When the jury holds no valid responses, every share is zero, the rule GJ-2 states for its own shares. The percentage renders as a percentage with one decimal place, with halves rounding up, the discipline GJ-2 and GJ-3 state.\n\nThe plurality of a jury is the offered answer holding the largest count among the jury valid responses, and it stands only when one answer holds that count alone. An exact tie for the largest count leaves no plurality standing, and a jury holding no valid responses holds no plurality, because its counts tie at zero. After the answer lines of a jury the plurality line stands, naming the word plurality, the model string, and the plurality answer, or the word none when no plurality stands for that jury.\n\nAfter the jury blocks of a section the agreement line stands. When the poll holds exactly two juries and both hold a plurality, the line names the word pluralities and then the word agree when the two plurality answers are the same answer and the word differ when they are not. In every other case the line names the word pluralities and then the words not counted. The closing line names the word agreements, then the count of the sections whose agreement line read agree, then the word of, then the count of the sections whose agreement line read agree or differ.\n\nSpoiled responses stand outside the shares, as they stand outside the shares of GJ-2, and they reach the reading only through the recorded and spoiled counts of the jury line. The reading is arithmetic over recorded responses and nothing more. It states shares, pluralities, and agreement counts and nothing else, and no line of it states or implies that a jury or a model did well or badly, because the reading carries no verdict about either jury. Every value the reading prints comes from a poll that loaded clean, so the one line rule FIX-GJ-6 states already covers each of them, and the reading builds no text of its own from a loaded value beyond the counts and the shares it computes.\n\nThe agreement reading of the forty recorded full polls, in poll order, stands at examples/full-agreement-golden.txt, produced by the agreement command over the forty poll files, and the script GJ-7 names regenerates it through the same command. Test, tests/test_agreement.py and tests/test_full.py."));
